You are building "Bounty Hunters" — a trading competition module for Adrena Protocol (Solana perp DEX).

## Project Context
Adrena is a perpetuals DEX on Solana (up to 100x leverage, SOL/BTC/BONK pairs). This module adds a bounty board where traders claim rewards by completing specific trading challenges (e.g., "Profit 5-10% on a SOL long in under 30 minutes").

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 14+ App Router with TypeScript (strict)
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Supabase for database + real-time subscriptions
- @solana/wallet-adapter-react for wallet connection
- @coral-xyz/anchor for Adrena program interaction
- framer-motion for animations
- lucide-react for icons

## Design System
- Theme: Dark (match app.adrena.xyz aesthetic)
- Background: #0a0a0f (near-black)
- Surface: #13131a (card backgrounds)
- Border: #1e1e2e (subtle borders)
- Primary accent: #00d4ff (electric blue)
- Success: #22c55e (green)
- Common tier: #22c55e (green glow)
- Rare tier: #a855f7 (purple glow)
- Legendary tier: #ffd700 (gold glow)
- Error/Expired: #ef4444 (red)
- Text primary: #e2e8f0
- Text secondary: #94a3b8
- Font headings: "Space Mono", monospace
- Font body: "Inter", sans-serif

## Code Conventions
- Server Components by default; "use client" only when needed (wallet, animations, real-time)
- All database calls go through src/lib/supabase.ts
- All Adrena data calls go through src/lib/adrena.ts
- Business logic lives in src/lib/, not in API routes or components
- Use Zod for API input validation
- Error boundaries on all dynamic components
- No "any" types ever

## Key Architecture Decisions
- Bounties are stored in Supabase, generated by a cron job (or manual trigger)
- Trade evaluation happens server-side by parsing Solana transaction logs
- Claims are first-come-first-served, verified against on-chain data
- Real-time updates via Supabase subscriptions (bounty status changes, new claims)
- Points-based scoring (no token distribution in prototype)

## File Organization
- src/app/ — Pages and API routes only
- src/components/ — Reusable UI components
- src/lib/ — Business logic, utilities, clients
- src/types/ — TypeScript type definitions
- src/hooks/ — Custom React hooks

## Adrena-Specific
- Program ID: 13gDzEXCdocbj8iAiqrScGo47NiSuYENGsRqi3SEAwet
- All trades are on-chain, no keeper model
- Parse close_position instruction logs for trade results
- Assets: SOL, BTC, BONK
- Leverage: up to 100x

## Priority
1. Make the bounty board LOOK incredible (this wins the demo)
2. Make the claim animation satisfying
3. Make the live feed feel alive
4. Backend correctness is secondary to frontend polish for the hackathon
